  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Showers and storms tapering off this morning \nbut more expected later this afternoon into this evening. \nShowers ending Monday morning.\n\nHeaviest rain since yesterday morning has been largely west \nof our area. The main issue earlier was Elk Co. Back edge of\nthe heavier rain is pulling to the east, thus expect most of\nthe activity to end from west to east by mid to late morning.\n\nClarion river running high but expected to remain below FS.\nWatching Beech Creek for a small band of moving across the\noffice now. Another small cluster of heavier showers just \nbrushing far southeast Lancaster Co.\n\nFocus later will be the potential for more showers and storms\nwith the cold front, mainly later this afternoon into this\nevening. Best dynamics look to be across the northwest.\n\nCooler and drier after early Monday.",
